# Pinned 0z0-shared ref that BOTH ci.yml and release.yml check out as the sibling
# ../0z0-shared dependency. SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH — bump it here only; both workflows
# read this file, so the two pins can no longer drift.
#
# A TAG, not a raw SHA. 0z0-shared releases every consumer-visible API change under a
# v-prefixed tag whose notes state what it breaks, so a pin bump is a legible diff and a
# reviewable decision. Read the notes for the tag being adopted before raising this.
#
# To bump: sync the local sibling clone to the new tag, re-run build + tests + the About
# window, then replace the tag below. Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored;
# the first non-comment line is the ref. Both workflows do a full `git clone` followed by
# `git checkout --detach <ref>`, which resolves a tag; a shallow clone would not, and would
# need `--branch <tag>` alongside `--depth 1`.
#
# ⚠ ADOPTING A NEW SHARED TYPE? BUMP THIS IN THE SAME PR. Local dev builds against the LIVE
# sibling checkout, so a new type resolves fine on the dev machine while CI — which clones the
# PINNED ref — fails with CS0234 "type does not exist in namespace ZeroZero.Brand.WinUI".
# That is exactly what happened: #59 adopted BrandAboutControl but left this pinned at
# 2d89d105 (which only had BrandAboutWindow), and CI stayed red from 2026-07-15 until 1.6.2.
# A green local build proves nothing about this pin.
v0.3.0
